{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-88228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality ${x}^{2}{e}^{2x-1}<-8{e}^{2x-1}-6x{e}^{2x-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-88228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{e}^{2x-1}<-8{e}^{2x-1}-6x{e}^{2x-1} \\\\ {x}^{2}{e}^{2x-1}+6x{e}^{2x-1}+8{e}^{2x-1} & <0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+6x+8){e}^{2x-1} & <0 \\\\ (x+4)(x+2){e}^{2x-1} & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${e}^{2x-1}$ and get\n\n$$\n(x+4)(x+2)<0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-4$ and $x=-2.$ The parabola is below the $x$-axis when $-4<x<-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/assets/15a31e60a938b604b96ade5e6868c658a2e2f0a53fe2a5f53a032093155e8aee.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-4<x<-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-88228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "872feb33a983cfba5d631e562226ad4131bcaa8306eeb901dd5477b03941598e"} {"question" "q-88228" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-88228" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3<x<3"] ["math" "-4<x<-2"] ["math" "2<x<4"] ["math" "x<3"] ["math" "x>-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-88228" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4<x<-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-88300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $-{3}^{6x+1}x<-{3}^{6x}{x}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-88300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{3}^{6x+1}x & <-{3}^{6x}{x}^{2} \\\\ {3}^{6x}{x}^{2}-{3}^{6x+1}x & <0 \\\\ {3}^{6x}({x}^{2}-3x) & <0 \\\\ {3}^{6x}x(x-3) & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${3}^{6x}$ and get\n\n$$\nx(x-3)<0.\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=0$ and $x=3.$ The parabola is below the $x$-axis when $0<x<3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/assets/8582e3a512cc29618a3e2db9dda4478481167eefcf0a2fbdfb7d33e5786ba62e.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is  $0<x<3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-88300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "872feb33a983cfba5d631e562226ad4131bcaa8306eeb901dd5477b03941598e"} {"question" "q-88300" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-88300" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0<x<3"] ["math" "x<3"] ["text" "$x<0$ or $x>3$"] ["text" "all real numbers"] ["text" "no solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-88300" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0<x<3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-88311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality ${x}^{3}\\cdot {5}^{7x}\\ge {5}^{7x-3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-88311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}\\cdot {5}^{7x} & \\ge {5}^{7x-3} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\cdot {5}^{7x}-{5}^{7x-3} & \\ge 0 \\\\ ({x}^{3}-{5}^{-3})\\cdot {5}^{7x} & \\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${5}^{7x}$ and get\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}-{5}^{-3}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & \\ge {5}^{-3} \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}} & \\ge \\sqrt[3]{{5}^{-3}} \\\\ x & \\ge {({5}^{-3})}^{1/3} \\\\ x & \\ge {5}^{-1} \\\\ x & \\ge \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is $x\\ge \\frac{1}{5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-88311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "872feb33a983cfba5d631e562226ad4131bcaa8306eeb901dd5477b03941598e"} {"question" "q-88311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-88311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{5}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "x\\ge -\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{1}{5}"] ["text" "$x\\le -\\frac{1}{5}$ or $x\\ge \\frac{1}{5}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-88311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\ge \\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-115431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $3x\\cdot {5}^{x+6}-{5}^{x+6}<8\\cdot {5}^{x+6}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-115431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x\\cdot {5}^{x+6}-{5}^{x+6} & <8\\cdot {5}^{x+6} \\\\ 3x\\cdot {5}^{x+6}-{5}^{x+6}-8\\cdot {5}^{x+6} & <0 \\\\ (3x-1-8){5}^{x+6} & <0 \\\\ (3x-9){5}^{x+6} & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${5}^{x+6}$ and solve the resulting inequality using familiar techniques:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-9 & <0 \\\\ 3x & <9 \\\\ x & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to the inequality above is $x<3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27fc400bbcf2762"} {"question" "q-115431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "872feb33a983cfba5d631e562226ad4131bcaa8306eeb901dd5477b03941598e"} {"question" "q-115431" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042952/state.json" "file_sha256" "e77c2eccdad30bf6f75e700e47e2a32105d11e04ad02fe7ef27